# ML models — training intermediates are noise, but the production ONNX
# models ship with the repo so the deploy image can bundle them. The
# margin .lgb mirror also ships: `Predictor::load` parses it for TreeSHAP
# attribution on the Predict page (see `crates/cstat-core/src/treeshap.rs`).
*.lgb
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.onnx
!/training/models/margin_model.onnx
!/training/models/win_model.onnx
!/training/models/margin_model.lgb
!/training/models/total_model.onnx
!/training/models/roster_model.onnx
!/training/models/roster_impact_model.onnx
!/training/models/roster_adjo_model.onnx
!/training/models/trajectory_mean_model.onnx
!/training/models/trajectory_q10_model.onnx
!/training/models/trajectory_q90_model.onnx
!/training/models/freshman_mean_model.onnx
!/training/models/freshman_q10_model.onnx
!/training/models/freshman_q90_model.onnx
!/training/models/pit_margin_model.onnx
!/training/models/pit_win_model.onnx
!/training/models/pit_total_model.onnx
!/training/models/pit_margin_model.lgb

# Training experiment side-by-side outputs. Results live in ROADMAP §4f;
# artifacts here are reproducible from the GBPM_VARIANT env var.
/training/models_experiments/

# Pre-retrain model snapshots — kept locally as a "before" reference when
# evaluating a retrain; git history holds the canonical "before" copy.
/training/models_*_backup/

# Training-pipeline CSV outputs (e.g. OOF predictions). Generated artifacts,
# not source — re-derivable from `python train.py`. Seed data for downstream
# work like the historical-prediction `game_forecasts` backfill.
/training/models/*.csv
# Same policy for nested experiment dirs (LOSO, future per-experiment dirs):
# per-game OOF dumps and ATS jsonl outputs are regeneratable from the LOSO
# pipeline; canonical summary numbers live in /training/eval_history/.
/training/models/**/*.csv
/training/models/**/*.jsonl
/training/models/pit_cam_v3_lookup.csv.gz
/training/models/oof_predictions_ats_summary.json
/training/models/loso/loso_pooled_ats_summary.json

# Per-team projection-backtest dumps. These are large (1 record/team-season;
# the 5-season dump is ~12k lines / 1.3k teams) and fully regenerable via
# `cstat-ingest projections-backtest --output PATH`. They were the source of
# huge PR diffs (89% of one PR). Keep the SUMMARY artifacts in eval_history
# (decomposition_*, q1_attribution_*, trajectory_attrition_* — small, the
# canonical sample-of-record) tracked; ignore the raw per-team dumps.
# Downstream diagnostics (decompose_projection_error.py,
# attribute_q1_overprojection.py) glob the newest local dump, so regenerate
# before re-running them.
/training/eval_history/projections_backtest_per_team_*.json

# Raw API snapshots from `cstat-ingest transfers` — bootstrap data dumped
# locally for repeatable seeds and offline dev. Re-derivable from the live
# 247 API. The canonical store is the `transfers` DB table.
/data/transfers/*_raw.json

# Raw HTML snapshots from `cstat-ingest recruits` — bootstrap data dumped
# locally for repeatable seeds and offline dev. Re-derivable from 247's
# composite recruit-rankings endpoint. Canonical store is the `recruits` DB table.
/data/recruits/*_raw.json

# Hand-generated PR diff dumps (e.g. `git diff main > pr.diff`) — useful
# for review locally, never meant to ship.
pr.diff

# Hand-written PR description draft — local scratch, never meant to ship.
pr.md

# Local scratch / investigation notes — text dumps, copy-pasted API
# responses, anything ending in _temp.txt. Never meant to ship.
*_temp.txt
*.scratch

# Railway / deploy runtime logs downloaded for debugging. Refreshed each
# time the container restarts, so committing them creates noisy diffs.
build.log
deploy.log

# Claude Code runtime state — machine-local, not part of the project.
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Logs
/logs/

# NatStat dashboard CSV exports for bulk season backfill. Per-season PBP
# files are ~725 MB each (over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit); even box-score
# CSVs total ~540 MB across 20 seasons and shouldn't ship in-repo. CSVs
# are intermediate — bulk-load into local Postgres, then they're optional
# to keep on disk. See ROADMAP "CSV bulk-bootstrap for historical seasons"
# and "Play-by-play ingestion".
/data/natstat_csv/
